# Common Mistakes

❌ I like wear T-shirt.

✅ I like **wearing** T-shirts.

---

❌ I buy cloth.

✅ I buy **clothes**.

---

❌ I make photos.

✅ I **take** photos.

---

❌ Fashion is very important for me.

✅ Fashion is fairly important to me, although I value comfort more.

---

# Band 8+ Tip

Always compare the past with the present when the question allows it.

### Example

> When I was younger, I didn't care much about fashion because my parents chose my clothes. However, now I pay more attention to dressing neatly since I often attend professional meetings and social events.

This comparison demonstrates a wider range of grammar and vocabulary.

